# Mode Transitions Handlers

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file defines specialized transition handlers and recovery protocols for mode transitions. It is part of the split mode-transitions documentation:

- **mode-transitions-core.md**: Essential transition definition and process
- **mode-transitions-handlers.md** (this file): Specialized transition handlers and recovery protocols
- **mode-transitions-context.md**: Context management during transitions

## Continuation Commands

After the initial transition, implementation can be guided or recovered using continuation commands:

1. **Continue Implementation**: `continue-implementation: @parameters/rules/dev-mode/continue-implementation.mdc`
   - Provides specific implementation guidance
   - Useful for complex implementation phases
   - Can specify different strategies for different phases

2. **Implementation Recovery**: `continue-implementation: @parameters/rules/helpers/recovery/recovery-strategy.mdc`
   - Helps recover from interrupted implementations
   - Provides focused recovery guidance
   - Maintains implementation context

## Advanced Workflow Examples

### Advanced Planning to Implementation Workflow

```
# Tyler initiates planning with specific template
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/template-advanced.mdc

# 1000xdev creates planning documentation
📋 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]
# ... planning activities ...

# 1000xdev signals planning completion
📋 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]
planning-document-complete

# Tyler initiates transition with implementation strategy
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/rules/dev-mode/log-based-implementation.mdc

# 1000xdev implements changes
💻 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]
# ... implementation activities ...

# Tyler provides additional guidance during implementation
continue-implementation: @parameters/rules/helpers/recovery/error-recovery.mdc

# 1000xdev continues implementation with new guidance
💻 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]
# ... additional implementation activities ...

# 1000xdev signals implementation completion
💻 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]
implementation-complete
```

